  "metadata": {
    "title": "The Sea Arch Light",
    "description": "A blue-and-white lighthouse standing on a sea arch: a rock out in the water that the waves have worn right through, so the sea runs under the lighthouse. There is no bridge; the keeper comes and goes by the rowing boat tied up under the ladder. Its lantern and window light up after dark in World View. 24 bricks.\n\n## How it is built\n\nEach step is a group in the Editor, so you can select it, delete it or build it again yourself.\n\n1. **Sea Arch** — two dark Block 2x2s stand two apart, and four dark Arches, one behind another, fill the gap between them, so the rock is 6 by 2 on top with a tunnel through the middle that the sea runs through. Rocks sit round its foot, clear of the tunnel's two mouths.\n2. **Landing** — a Ladder up the south face of the west block from the water, and a dark Half Cube on top for a bollard to tie up to.\n3. **Boat** — a red Plate 2x4 hull turned 90° (press **R**), a Bench across it for the seat, and two Trims for oars, moored at the foot of the ladder.\n4. **Tower** — a white Block 2x2 on the east block, then a blue Pillar on top, so the tower narrows as it rises. The blue Door, turned 90°, faces back across the top of the arch to the ladder; a Small Window in the blue band glows with lamplight at night.\n5. **Lantern** — a Round Plate 2x2, a Lantern that lights up after dark, another Round Plate 2x2 and a blue Cone Roof.\n\nStand it out in open water, away from the shore, so the boat is the only way there, and leave room for the sea to run through the arch.\n\n## Bricks\n\n- Sea Arch: 2 Block 2x2, 4 Arch, 4 Rock\n- Landing: 1 Ladder, 1 Half Cube\n- Boat: 1 Plate 2x4, 1 Bench, 2 Trim\n- Tower: 1 Block 2x2, 1 Pillar, 1 Door, 1 Small Window\n- Lantern: 2 Round Plate 2x2, 1 Lantern, 1 Cone Roof\n\n24 bricks in all.\n",
